.. raw:: html

    <div class="sphx-glr-thumbcontainer" tooltip="With only a handful of measurements, the standardized mean t = (\bar x - \mu_0)/(s/\sqrt n) is not normal: estimating the spread from the same small sample gives it heavier tails. Gosset (&quot;Student&quot;, 1908) derived its exact distribution. This example shows the heavy tails, how a normal cutoff misleads for small samples, and the one- and two-sample t-tests built on Student&#x27;s distribution.">

